# cjk-sc: Han, kana, Hangul and full-width punctuation, with Han in the
# forms Simplified Chinese uses, as mainland China and Singapore write them,
# from Noto Sans CJK SC. A font set adds this layer after Noto Sans Mono,
# which holds none of them. Each character is two cells wide, and the font
# draws at its own size.
#
# Unicode encodes each Han character once, even where China, Taiwan, Japan
# and Korea each write it in a slightly different form, such as 直, 骨 and
# 刃. Noto Sans CJK holds each region's forms in a face of its own, so the
# catalog has one layer for each region, and a set holds one of them.
# Distributions install the faces as one collection, NotoSansCJK-Regular.ttc.
#
# License: SIL OFL 1.1.
#
# References:
# - ADR-1204 D5: the script layers.
# - ADR-1204 D6: a set holds one Han face at most.

role=script
source=font:Noto Sans CJK SC
version=2.004
url=https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk/releases/tag/Sans2.004
